course: dictionary
lesson: 11958
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning. The word carving can mean a made object, the art of making it, or cutting cooked meat. To know which one is right, read the words around it: they are its context. «The museum has a stone carving of a lion.» Stone and museum tell you a carving is an object, like a statue.
explain: «Dad used the carving knife to cut the roast.» Carving knife, cut and roast are clues. They tell you carving means cutting cooked meat into slices. Always ask: which meaning fits this sentence? Then try it in place of the word and see if it still makes sense.
explain: Carving can also mean the art or activity of cutting shapes into wood or stone. «Mia loves wood carving, so every week she carves a little bird.» Loves and carves show that carving is something Mia does for fun. Carve is the verb: she carves, they carved, they are carving.
fact: Context means the words and sentences around a word.
fact: «Carving» can mean an object made by cutting, such as a stone carving or a pumpkin carving.
fact: «Carving» can also mean the art or activity of cutting shapes into a material, such as wood carving.
fact: «Carving» can mean cutting cooked meat into slices, as with a carving knife.
fact: «Carve» is the verb: she carves, they carved, they are carving.
exercise: «Dad used the carving knife to cut the roast chicken.» What is carving in this sentence? | Washing up after dinner | Painting a picture | Growing vegetables in the garden | *Cutting cooked meat into slices
exercise: «The museum has a stone carving of a lion.» What is a carving here? | A kind of boat | *An object made by cutting stone | A cooked meat dinner | A painted wall
exercise: «Mia loves wood carving, and every week she carves a little bird.» Find and copy the verb form of carving in this sentence. | wood | bird | *carves | every
test: «The totem pole had a carving of an eagle at the top.» What is a carving here? | A loud noise | A type of bird that flies | Cutting meat into slices | *An object made by cutting wood
test: Which phrase from the lessons names a tool used to cut the roast? | stone carving | wood carving | *carving knife | pumpkin carving
exam: «Grandma carved the turkey at the table.» What does carved mean here? | *Cut cooked meat into slices | Wrote a letter | Painted the table | Sang a happy song
